---
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<section class="section" id="maven" aria-labelledby="maven-heading">
  <div class="shell editorial-layout">
    <header class="section-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">POWERED BY MAVENJ</p>
      <h2 class="section-heading" id="maven-heading">Maven Projects. Zero Friction.</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="editorial-copy">
      <p class="body-copy">Open an existing Maven project and start writing Java. TurboJ resolves dependencies, understands modules, and provides code intelligence without running a full Maven build after every edit.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Work across modules, run JUnit tests, and keep the project's Java version and toolchain settings. A compact project explorer keeps source, tests, and dependencies close at hand.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Fast Compile keeps the editing loop moving. Explicit Maven Build commands run the project's full lifecycle when you need its plugins and build phases.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">MavenJ is an independent Java library, embedded directly in TurboJ and reusable by other tools and coding agents.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${site.links.source}/tree/main/mavenj`}>Explore MavenJ source and documentation</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .text-link { color: var(--tj-ui-link); display: inline-block; margin-top: 12px; }
</style>
